<title>ITALY: Italy's Venice sees Dec CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Venice sees Dec CPI at 3.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>VENICE, Italy 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Venice said its December consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 3.0 percent year on year.</p>
<p>In November, the Venice inflation rate was 0.4 percent and 3.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Venice is one of 10 Italian cities which published inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 7.89 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to November 1996):</p>
<p>					  Month/Month	Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		   0.2   (0.4)	3.0  (3.0)</p>
<p>    Food				0.2  (-0.4)	2.2  (2.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	 0.0   (0.3)	4.1  (4.5)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges 0.3   (1.0)	4.7  (4.9)</p>
<p>    Furniture			 0.2   (0.2)	3.5  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		 0.0   (0.0)	1.1  (1.0)</p>
<p>    Transportation		  0.2   (0.7)	3.5  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture   0.4   (0.1)     -2.0 (-2.3)</p>
<p>    Education			 0.0   (4.8)	5.0  (8.0)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants     -0.3   (1.2)	8.4  (9.0)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services     0.1  (-0.5)	0.4  (0.5)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129589</p>
